#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exception

#% text
# `exception(type, data)` is an exception of the given type, with an association of data: a plain value that `throw_exception` can throw.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `exception(type)` has no data; data that is not an association is kept under the key `payload`.

#% item
# An exception is a value, not a failure, so it can be passed to functions, stored and inspected: `exception_type`, `exception_data`, `exception_tags`. Throwing it makes a failure that propagates until `catch_exception`, as `throw` does.

#% item
# The types are symbols or strings; `register_exception_type(type, parent)` makes a type a kind of another, so that catching the parent also catches it.

#% item
# Exceptions are ordinary terms over the failures and `throw`/`catch` of the core, not a separate mechanism with messages (semantics 10).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42))
#% output
#= exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42))

#% cell
exception_data(exception(data_error, assoc(data -> 42)))
#% output
#= assoc(data -> 42)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# With a hierarchy of types:

#% cell
register_exception_type(arg_error)
register_exception_type(arg_type_error, arg_error)
exception_tags(exception(arg_type_error))
#% output
#= [arg_type_error, arg_error]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Catching by a parent type:

#% cell
register_exception_type(arg_error)
register_exception_type(arg_type_error, arg_error)
catch_exception(1 + throw_exception(exception(arg_type_error, assoc(value -> pi))), arg_error)
#% output
#= exception(arg_type_error, assoc(value -> pi))

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A type may be a string or a number, and without data the exception has an empty data association; a call without a type stays as it is:

#% cell
[exception("s", assoc(a -> 1)), exception("s"), exception()]
#% output
#= [exception("s", assoc(a -> 1)), exception("s", assoc()), exception()]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `throw_exception`, `catch_exception`, `register_exception_type`, `throw`, `catch`
